# A background Bash task: how the footer shows it, /tasks while it runs, and quitting while it runs.
quiet 3000 20000
send Use the Bash tool with run_in_background set to true to run the command: sleep 90. Do not wait for it. Then reply with exactly STARTED.
sleep 200
send \r
wait 90000 \x07
quiet 3000 20000
sleep 3000
send /tasks
sleep 200
send \r
quiet 2500 10000
send \x1b
quiet 2000 10000
send \x03
quiet 2000 8000
send \x03
quiet 3000 10000
exit 10000
